<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36146" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phŏrōneus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trisyll.</span></b> ), ĕi and
			ĕos, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φορωνεύς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>son of Inachus</i>, <i>king of
			Argos</i>, <i>and brother of Io</i>, <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				124</span></i>; <i><span class="en">143</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">225</span></i>; 274; <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 56,
				57, § 193</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 4,
				889</span></i>. —Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phŏrōnēus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>Phoronean</i>, <b>poet.</b> for <i>Argive</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phoroneis sub antris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 3, 2, 101</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phŏrō-nis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f.
			adj., <i>Phoronean</i>, <b>poet.</b> for <i>Argive</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phoronides latuere venae,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the river Inachus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Thyest. 115</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phorōnis</span></b> ,
			ĭdis, f., <i>Io</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 1, 668</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2,
		524</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
